step Get the route suitability data from a balise
sub SubStep 1 - Receive the data
telegram balise Q_UPDOWN=1 M_VERSION=32 Q_MEDIA=0 N_PIG=0 N_TOTAL=0 M_DUP=0 M_MCOUNT=1 NID_C=85 NID_BG=258 Q_LINK=0 | ROUTE_SUITABILITY_DATA NID_PACKET=70 Q_DIR=2 L_PACKET=1 Q_SCALE=1 Q_TRACKINIT=0 D_SUITABILITY=700 Q_SUITABILITY=2 M_VOLTAGE=5 NID_CTRACTION=85 N_ITER=2 D_SUITABILITY=400 Q_SUITABILITY=2 M_VOLTAGE=1 NID_CTRACTION=85 D_SUITABILITY=1000 Q_SUITABILITY=1 M_AXLELOADCAT=4
sub Sub-step 2 - Check the unsuitabilities are recorded
expect efs: (COUNT X IN Kernel.TrackDescription.RouteSuitability.RouteSuitabilityProfile.Items) == 3 @ deadline=1
expect efs: Kernel.TrackDescription.RouteSuitability.IsUnsuitable (FIRST X IN Kernel.TrackDescription.RouteSuitability.RouteSuitabilityProfile.Items) == Boolean.True @ deadline=1
expect efs: Kernel.TrackDescription.RouteSuitability.IsUnsuitable (LAST X IN Kernel.TrackDescription.RouteSuitability.RouteSuitabilityProfile.Items) == Boolean.True @ deadline=1
expect efs: THERE_IS X IN Kernel.TrackDescription.RouteSuitability.RouteSuitabilityProfile.Items | Kernel.TrackDescription.RouteSuitability.IsUnsuitable( anItem=> X ) == Boolean.False @ deadline=1
step Expectations
sub SubStep 1 - The unsuitabilities are displayed on the DMI
expect efs: (COUNT X IN DMI.MasterDMI().Out_RouteUnsuitabilities.RouteUnsuitabilities) == 2 @ deadline=1
expect efs: DMI.MasterDMI().Out_RouteUnsuitabilities.OutputInformation.DisplayRequested == Boolean.True @ deadline=1
sub Sub-step 2 - Start of the closest unsuitability is considered EOA with no release speed
expect efs: Kernel.MA.EOA.EOA().Location != BaseTypes.Distance.Infinity @ deadline=1
expect efs: Kernel.MA.EOA.EOA().Location == 795.0 @ deadline=1
expect efs: Kernel.MA.EOA.EOA().Speed == 0.0 @ deadline=1
sub Sub-step 3 - Start of the closest unsuitability is considered SvL
expect efs: Kernel.MA.SvL.SvL().Location == 795.0 @ deadline=1
sequence Handle route suitability data from a balise - All correct
